{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Every native-born person shall do thus.</b> Why is this stated? Since it says ״ומעוך וכתות״ etc. — these you do not accept, but you do accept from them unblemished ones. Once I have merited that the inhabitant of the land (הא״י) brings a burnt-offering, one might think: just as Israel brings libations, so too the Canaanite brings libations — Scripture says, ״כל האזרח יעשה ככה״ etc.: Israel brings libations, but the Canaanite does not bring libations. From here they said: a gentile who sent his burnt-offerings from abroad and did not send libations with them, they are offered from public funds."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The abbreviation הא״י is resolved here as הארץ ישראל; the following כנעני/Canaanite then refers to a non-Israelite resident of the land."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:06.089238967Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}